<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-8930] ODBC: Cursors are not closed when used through Go</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8930</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Client used:&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/alexbrainman/odbc&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/alexbrainman/odbc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example app for reproducing: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/nombiezinja/ignite-cursor-example&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/nombiezinja/ignite-cursor-example&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After several execution of statements user begins to get the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;2018/06/29 20:46:06 SQLExecute: {HY000} Too many open cursors (either close
other open cursors or increase the limit through
ClientConnectorConfiguration.maxOpenCursorsPerConnection) [maximum=128,
current=128]&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
